I like tycoon games and I played Game Dev Tycoon. Mad Games Tycoon is very similar. You will recognize many features of Game Dev Tycoon within the game, but it is a somewhat different approach.
You start in a little garage with no rooms visible except your car and a desk with a computer. You have to build rooms, get new staff members and manage their needs (although this part of the game comes rather short).
And of course, you have to develop games for the PC or any other console, which is available at the given time. This looks very similar to Game Dev Tycoon, which is not bad, because I loved how creating new games works in Game Dev Tycoon.
To give Game Dev Tycoon as a reference is not always fair, because although both games share the same genre and topic, they both are intend to be different from each other and that is good for both games.
I like Mad Games Tycoon, because ...
... it is very intuitive (you do not really need a tutorial);
... it has nice graphics, which perfectly fit to the game concept;
... it keeps me seated at the computer with the question in mind "I want to know what comes next!" -> is good!
... it offers the chance to be creative and try many ideas for new games;
... it offers a challenge in really be able to work up a small gaming industry into a large and well-known company with many fans;
... it can be easy, so you do not neccessarily feel stressed when you play the game (easy mode);
... it can be harder, but not too hard, when you want to have a more challenging game experience;
... it shows potential in some aspects, which are worked on, because I have only played the early access version yet.

Alright, so i will not rate this game more so because i honestly believe the idea is GREAT.  Seriously i felt like it was real but the graphics, the mechanics and some issues are what is seriously hampering the games progress.  I recommend a revamp on the game to build it up for an official release.
To the creator/team;
You guys are great for putting forth a game that not many people could make.  Just my advice being an avid gamer is try to not rush things.  You can see that games like GTA V and other big titles are taking their time either because of competition or because they feel they can fix things for a great release.  You are on the right track and i hope to expect more from you all.
